    "importer": {
      "answer": "Both previously failing importer tests now pass, and the suite is green.\n\n## Files re-read (current, not historical)\n- `docs/api.txt` — authoritative v1 contract for `import_rows` (normalize id via strip+NFC, never lowercase; reject empty id / invalid timestamp / invalid revision; aware timestamp → UTC date, naive = UTC, `Z` valid; dedup by normalized id keeping highest revision, last wins at tie; no mutation, no global state; empty → `[]`).\n- `importer.py` — was the stub: `[{\"id\": r[\"id\"], \"day\": r[\"timestamp\"][:10], ...}]`.\n- `parser.py` — unchanged, still the Decimal-based `parse_amount`.\n- `tests/test_public.py` — 4 tests.\n\n## Baseline before edits\n```\nexit=1 — FAILED (failures=2)\ntest_dedup: 2 != 1\ntest_utc:   {'2026-10-12': 200} != {'2026-10-11': 200}\n```\n\n## Change\nEdited **only `importer.py`** (`import_rows` plus small helpers). `parser.py` and `report.py` untouched.\n- `_normalize_id`: must be str, `strip()` then `unicodedata.normalize(\"NFC\", ...)`, no lowercasing; empty → `ValueError`.\n- `_utc_day`: `datetime.fromisoformat` with `Z` accepted, naive treated as UTC, aware converted via `astimezone(utc)`, then `date().isoformat()` — this fixes the `+02:00` case rolling back a day.\n- `_revision`: non-negative int only (bools rejected), default 0.\n- Dedup with a `seen` dict + insertion `order` list; keep highest revision, `>=` so last input wins at equal revision; builds fresh dicts so no input mutation, and all state is call-local.\n\n## Post-edit test run (actual)\n```\nexit=0\ntest_dedup ............. ok\ntest_money ............. ok\ntest_negative_rounding . ok\ntest_utc ............... ok\nRan 4 tests — OK\n```\nNo remaining importer failures. Per the phase boundary I did not touch `report.py`; `running_balance`/`report_metadata` remain report-phase work and are still unimplemented. Stopping here.",
